# Store every file byte-for-byte. No newline conversion, no charset guessing.
#
# This is deliberate and load-bearing. CLAUDE.md records four separate occasions where an
# encoding transform silently corrupted this project - a BOM that broke skill discovery, an
# ANSI read that shredded 22 techniques, an em-dash that became a parser error. Git's default
# on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) is another such transform. Turning it off here stops version
# control from becoming the fifth trap.
#
# The cost is that a file authored with CRLF stays CRLF in the repo. That is the correct
# trade: the scripts are pure ASCII and the validators read with explicit encoding, so byte
# fidelity matters far more here than newline tidiness.
* -text

# Mark the deliverable binary so git never attempts a textual diff on it.
*.pdf binary
